Source: netavark
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Reinhard Tartler <siretart@tauware.de>
# No librust-*-dev crate build-dependencies on purpose: all crates are
# vendored from crates.io at build time (see debian/rules and
# debian/fetch-vendor.sh), because deepin's packaged crate versions are
# too old for netavark.  protobuf-compiler is a plain C++ tool needed by
# the vendored prost-build 0.14 for build.rs (>= 3.15): on sid it came
# in transitively via librust-prost-build-dev, with vendored crates apt
# no longer pulls it in, so it must be declared explicitly.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 14),
               dh-sequence-single-binary,
               cargo:native <!nocheck>,
               rustc:native (>= 1.86) <!nocheck>,
               libstd-rust-dev <!nocheck>,
               protobuf-compiler <!nocheck>
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/containers/netavark
Vcs-Browser: https://salsa.debian.org/debian/netavark
Vcs-Git: https://salsa.debian.org/debian/netavark.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: netavark
Architecture: any
Provides: container-network-stack (= 2)
Recommends: aardvark-dns, nftables
Breaks: aardvark-dns (<< 1.12)
Enhances: podman
Description: Rust based network stack for containers
 Netavark is designed to work with but is also applicable
 for other OCI container management applications.
